      <strong>Create </strong><strong><code>topics/recording-is-silent.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE troubleshooting PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Troubleshooting//EN\" \"troubleshooting.dtd\">\n\n\u003ctroubleshooting id=\"recording-is-silent\">\n  \u003ctitle>The recording is silent\u003c/title>\n  \u003cshortdesc>You pressed Record but the waveform is a flat line and playback is silent: the input device, its level or its permissions are wrong.\u003c/shortdesc>\n  \u003cprolog>\n    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n    \u003ccritdates>\n      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-02-20\"/>\n    \u003c/critdates>\n    \u003cmetadata>\n      \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"novice\"/>\n      \u003ccategory>troubleshooting\u003c/category>\n      \u003ckeywords>\n        \u003ckeyword>silent recording\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003ckeyword>flat line\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003ckeyword>microphone\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003cindexterm>troubleshooting\u003cindexterm>silent recording\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n        \u003cindexterm>microphone\u003cindexterm>not detected\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n      \u003c/keywords>\n    \u003c/metadata>\n  \u003c/prolog>\n  \u003ctroublebody>\n    \u003ccondition>\n      \u003ctitle>Condition\u003c/title>\n      \u003cp>You click \u003cuicontrol>Record\u003c/uicontrol>, the track appears, but the waveform stays a flat line.\n      Playing the track produces no sound.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/condition>\n    \u003ctroubleSolution>\n      \u003ccause>\n        \u003ctitle>The wrong input device is selected\u003c/title>\n        \u003cp>The \u003cuicontrol>Device Toolbar\u003c/uicontrol> is set to a device that is not connected, or to a line input rather than the microphone.\u003c/p>\n      \u003c/cause>\n      \u003cremedy>\n        \u003ctitle>Select the microphone\u003c/title>\n        \u003csteps>\n          \u003cstep>\n            \u003ccmd>Click \u003cuicontrol>Stop\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/cmd>\n          \u003c/step>\n          \u003cstep>\n            \u003ccmd>In the \u003cuicontrol>Device Toolbar\u003c/uicontrol>, open the recording device list and choose your microphone.\u003c/cmd>\n          \u003c/step>\n          \u003cstep>\n            \u003ccmd>Choose \u003cmenucascade>\u003cuicontrol>Transport\u003c/uicontrol>\u003cuicontrol>Rescan Audio Devices\u003c/uicontrol>\u003c/menucascade> if the microphone is missing from the list.\u003c/cmd>\n          \u003c/step>\n        \u003c/steps>\n      \u003c/remedy>\n    \u003c/troubleSolution>\n    \u003ctroubleSolution>\n      \u003ccause>\n        \u003ctitle>The input level is zero\u003c/title>\n        \u003cp>The recording volume slider is at its minimum, so the device is selected but nothing is captured.\u003c/p>\n      \u003c/cause>\n      \u003cremedy>\n        \u003ctitle>Raise the recording volume\u003c/title>\n        \u003csteps>\n          \u003cstep>\n            \u003ccmd>Drag the recording volume slider (the one with the microphone icon) to about three quarters.\u003c/cmd>\n          \u003c/step>\n          \u003cstep>\n            \u003ccmd>Click the recording meter to start monitoring, then speak; the meter should move.\u003c/cmd>\n          \u003c/step>\n        \u003c/steps>\n      \u003c/remedy>\n    \u003c/troubleSolution>\n    \u003ctroubleSolution platform=\"mac\">\n      \u003ccause>\n        \u003ctitle>macOS has not granted microphone access\u003c/title>\n        \u003cp>The first time an application asks to use the microphone, macOS asks for permission.\n        If the request was refused, \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> records silence.\u003c/p>\n      \u003c/cause>\n      \u003cremedy>\n        \u003ctitle>Allow microphone access\u003c/title>\n        \u003csteps-informal>\n          \u003cp>Open \u003cmenucascade>\u003cuicontrol>System Settings\u003c/uicontrol>\u003cuicontrol>Privacy and Security\u003c/uicontrol>\u003cuicontrol>Microphone\u003c/uicontrol>\u003c/menucascade>, switch on \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>, then restart it.\u003c/p>\n        \u003c/steps-informal>\n      \u003c/remedy>\n    \u003c/troubleSolution>\n  \u003c/troublebody>\n  \u003crelated-links>\n    \u003clink href=\"recording-your-first-track.dita\"/>\n    \u003clink href=\"preparing-to-record.dita\"/>\n  \u003c/related-links>\n\u003c/troubleshooting>"} lang="xml" title="topics/recording-is-silent.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the structure</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>The DOCTYPE is <code>-//OASIS//DTD DITA Troubleshooting//EN</code> with <code>troubleshooting.dtd</code>; the body is <code>&lt;troublebody&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;condition&gt;</code> describes the symptom the reader sees. It takes a <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> and body elements.</li>
      <li>Each <code>&lt;troubleSolution&gt;</code> pairs one <code>&lt;cause&gt;</code> with one <code>&lt;remedy&gt;</code>, in that order; the DTD does not let a remedy come first. A topic may have as many solutions as it has plausible causes; put the most likely first.</li>
      <li>A <code>&lt;remedy&gt;</code> must say what to do as <code>&lt;steps&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;steps-unordered&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;steps-informal&gt;</code>. The first two remedies are proper <code>&lt;steps&gt;</code>, the same element as in a task; the macOS remedy is one paragraph in <code>&lt;steps-informal&gt;</code>. A remedy with only a <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> does not validate, as the demo at the end shows.</li>
      <li>The third solution carries <code>platform="mac"</code>. The profiling attributes from stage 14 work on <code>&lt;troubleSolution&gt;</code> as on any element, so the Windows and Linux builds drop the macOS solution and <code>validate-conditions</code> checks the value against the subject scheme.</li>
      <li>The <code>&lt;prolog&gt;</code> follows the stage 13 policy: a creator, a created date, an audience, a category and keywords, with two nested <code>&lt;indexterm&gt;</code>s so the topic is in the book's index under both <em>troubleshooting</em> and <em>microphone</em>.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the trouble note</strong> The recording task changes one note:
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n+++ b/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n@@ -63,8 +63,8 @@\n         \u003ccmd>Click \u003cuicontrol>Record\u003c/uicontrol>, or press \u003cuicontrol>R\u003c/uicontrol>, to start recording.\u003c/cmd>\n         \u003cinfo>\n           \u003cp>A blue waveform appears as \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> captures audio from your microphone, like \u003cxref href=\"what-is-digital-audio.dita#what-is-digital-audio/fig-waveform\"/>.\u003c/p>\n-          \u003cnote type=\"warning\">A flat line instead of a waveform means the microphone is not selected correctly.\n-          Click \u003cuicontrol>Stop\u003c/uicontrol> and check the recording device.\u003c/note>\n+          \u003cnote type=\"trouble\">A flat line instead of a waveform means nothing is being captured.\n+          See \u003cxref href=\"recording-is-silent.dita\"/>.\u003c/note>\n         \u003c/info>\n       \u003c/step>\n       \u003cstep>"} lang="diff" title="topics/recording-your-first-track.dita" />
      <p><code>&lt;note type="trouble"&gt;</code> is the note type for "if this goes wrong, look here". The HTML5 transform labels it <em>Trouble:</em>. It replaces a <code>warning</code>, which is for harm to people or data, and the fix moves out of the note into the topic it links to. The <code>&lt;xref&gt;</code> is a plain local reference; the book, the beginner guide and the podcaster guide all contain the target, so it resolves in every deliverable.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-2-the-topic-in-every-map" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 2: The topic in every map<a href="#step-2-the-topic-in-every-map" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>audacity-guide.ditamap</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/audacity-guide.ditamap\n+++ b/audacity-guide.ditamap\n@@ -51,6 +51,10 @@\n       \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/removing-background-noise.dita\" linking=\"targetonly\"/>\n       \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/effect-order.dita\"/>\n     \u003c/topicset>\n+  \u003c/topichead>\n+\n+  \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Troubleshooting\" id=\"troubleshooting\">\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/recording-is-silent.dita\" keys=\"silent\"/>\n   \u003c/topichead>\n \n   \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Podcast production\" audience=\"podcaster\">"} lang="diff" title="audacity-guide.ditamap" />
      </Step>
