      <h2 id="step-3-readme-and-the-gate" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 3: README and the gate<a href="#step-3-readme-and-the-gate" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Change the "You are on" line</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n Build a guide through 27 stages. Maps begin at stage 02; HTML publication begins at stage 03.\n \n-You are on stage 19: bookmap.\n+You are on stage 20: troubleshooting.\n \n ## Stages\n "} lang="diff" title="README.md" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Format and check</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita *.ditamap\nscripts/check-stage.sh"} lang="bash" />
      <CodeBlock code={"== validate-project  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\n39 file(s): 39 valid, 0 invalid.\n\n== project-health  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\nRoot map: audacity-guide.ditamap (project config); house rules: none (none configured)\nProject is healthy: valid, no broken references, keys, orphans, or broken element ids.\n\n== validate-conditions  /home/you/audacity-guide  (scheme: subject-scheme.ditamap) ==\n39 file(s): 39 pass, 0 with violations.\n\n== build  project.json -> /tmp/check-stage-\u003cpid> ==\nall deliverables built\n\nSTAGE OK"} lang="plaintext" />
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p>Test the content model for a remedy. In the macOS solution, replace the <code>&lt;steps-informal&gt;</code> element with its <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> alone, so that <code>&lt;remedy&gt;</code> holds a title and a paragraph, and run the gate with <code>SKIP_BUILD=1</code>:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"== validate-project  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\n/home/you/audacity-guide/topics/recording-is-silent.dita:\n  76:16  error: The content of element type \"remedy\" does not match its content model.\n39 file(s): 38 valid, 1 invalid.\nFAIL: validation errors"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p><code>&lt;remedy&gt;</code> allows an optional <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>, then one of <code>&lt;steps&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;steps-unordered&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;steps-informal&gt;</code>, and nothing else. What to do is always a steps element, even when it is one sentence: that is what <code>&lt;steps-informal&gt;</code> is for.</p>
      <p>After each error exercise, undo the deliberate change and rerun the gate. Confirm that it prints <code>STAGE OK</code> before continuing.</p>
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;troubleshooting&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;troublebody&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;condition&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;troubleSolution&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;cause&gt;</code> then <code>&lt;remedy&gt;</code>; a remedy's content is <code>&lt;steps&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;steps-unordered&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;steps-informal&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>A profiling attribute on a <code>&lt;troubleSolution&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;note type="trouble"&gt;</code> with an <code>&lt;xref&gt;</code> to the troubleshooting topic, in place of a warning that carried the fix itself.</li>
      <li>One topic referenced by five maps, including a nested reference in a branch-filtered map.</li>
      </ul>
